# Stage 1 replication (PROPOSAL 362b16c, frozen by the Advisor 2026-11-10): held-out, S1 only, plain payload, cut 0.9,
# arms N/V0/VG/I1/I2b; cells 1.7B MATH-500 250, 8B GSM8K 250, 8B MATH-500 100 (the Stage 0 8B MATH pool). FULL traces:
# the Stage 0 held-out stores, bundled byte-identical (FULL_CHECK; every selected item has its FULL, none generated).
# Needs the user's own approval line in the Executor pane. Readings: selfdoubt/stage1_rep.py.
# Rates measured in Stage 0 CONT (all cuts; x0.93 central for cut 0.9 as measured on GSM8K, x0.80 ceiling):
#   1.7B MATH 573 tok/s, 8B GSM8K 874, 8B MATH 313. Tokens/item from Stage 0 cut-0.9 rows: ceiling N+U0+UG+2*U0
#   (1.7B MATH 11,621; 8B GSM8K 4,052; 8B MATH 12,936); central x the S1/S0 per-arm ratios measured on 1.7B GSM8K.
#   Step ceilings: 1.7B MATH 6,400 s; 8B GSM8K 1,600 s; 8B MATH 5,300 s (each incl. ~90 s model load). Setup ~200 s.
# TWO PODS, pod A (launch first): Qwen3-1.7B MATH-500 250.
# Central ~4,300 s (1 h 11 min, $0.70); ceiling ~6,600 s (1 h 50 min, $1.08); hard DELETE at 8,250 s = 2 h 17.5 min
#   ($1.35 at $0.59/h; ~$1.39 with disk).
